{% block content %}{% raw %}
<section class="tour-hero">
        <h1>East Nusa Penida Tour</h1>
        <p style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:10px;">Panoramic Vistas and Iconic Photo Spots</p>
    </section>

    <main class="tour-container">
        <div class="tour-grid">
            <div class="tour-description">
                <p style="font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:30px;color:#444;">Venture to the spectacular eastern shores of Nusa Penida. This private day trip is designed for those seeking breathtaking coastal views, iconic photo opportunities, and the raw beauty of Bali's neighboring island. From the gleaming white sands of Diamond Beach to the famous Molenteng Tree House, our experienced team ensures a comfortable, safe, and truly memorable journey.</p>
                
                <h2 class="section-heading">Tour Itinerary</h2>
                <ul class="itinerary-list">
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-car"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>06:30 AM – Hotel Pick-up</h3><p>Private transfer from your Bali hotel to Sanur Harbor.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-ship"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>07:30 AM – Fast Boat to Nusa Penida</h3><p>High-speed boat transfer across the beautiful Badung Strait.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-umbrella-beach"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>09:30 AM – Atuh Beach</h3><p>Arrive and explore the beautiful, secluded Atuh Beach.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-camera"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>10:30 AM – Thousand Island Viewpoint</h3><p>Take in the breathtaking Raja Lima panoramic ocean vistas.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-tree"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>11:30 AM – Molenteng Tree House</h3><p>Visit the famous Rumah Pohon for an iconic vacation photo.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-utensils"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>01:30 PM – Lunch</h3><p>Enjoy a delicious local lunch featuring Balinese or Western foods.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-gem"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>02:30 PM – Diamond Beach</h3><p>Walk along the stunning white sands and towering karst formations.</p></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="itinerary-item">
                        <div class="itinerary-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-car-side"></i></div>
                        <div class="itinerary-details"><h3>05:30 PM – Return to Bali</h3><p>Fast boat back to Sanur Harbor, then private drop-off at your hotel.</p></div>
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <div class="tour-gallery">
                    <h2>Tour Gallery</h2>
                    <div class="gallery-grid">
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/diamond-beach.webp" alt="Diamond Beach white sand and turquoise water, East Nusa Penida" fetchpriority="high" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/diamond-beach-swing.webp" alt="Swing at Diamond Beach with ocean views" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/tree-house.webp" alt="Molenteng Tree House iconic photo spot, Nusa Penida" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/tree-house-view.webp" alt="View from Molenteng Tree House, Nusa Penida" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/nusa-penida-thousand-island-view-point.webp" alt="Thousand Islands viewpoint Raja Lima, East Nusa Penida" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/atuh-beach.webp" alt="Atuh Beach crystal clear water, East Nusa Penida" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/stunning-atuh-beach.webp" alt="Aerial view of stunning Atuh Beach" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                        <div class="gallery-item"><img src="src/assets/penida/thousand-islands.webp" alt="Thousand Islands rock formations East Nusa Penida" loading="lazy" width="300" height="225"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-question">What is the difference between East and West Nusa Penida tours? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i></button>
                    <div class="faq-answer"><p>West Nusa Penida is known for dramatic cliff formations like Kelingking Beach and Broken Beach. East Nusa Penida offers panoramic coastal vistas, Diamond Beach, Atuh Beach, and the iconic Molenteng Tree House — generally less crowded and more serene.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-question">Can I combine East and West Nusa Penida in one day? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i></button>
                    <div class="faq-answer"><p>Combining both coasts in a single day is very tiring due to the island's road conditions. We strongly recommend booking each as a separate day trip to enjoy the experience fully and comfortably.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-question">Is Diamond Beach worth visiting? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i></button>
                    <div class="faq-answer"><p>Absolutely. Diamond Beach is consistently ranked among the most beautiful beaches in Indonesia. The white sand, crystal-clear turquoise water, and striking diamond-shaped karst rock formations make it a world-class photography destination.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-question">What should I bring on the East Nusa Penida tour? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i></button>
                    <div class="faq-answer"><p>Bring comfortable closed-toe shoes (for the staircase descents), reef-safe sunscreen, a hat, camera, and some cash. We provide bottled water and lunch throughout the day.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-question">What is included in the East Nusa Penida tour price? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i></button>
                    <div class="faq-answer"><p>The all-inclusive price covers private A/C transport, return fast boat tickets from Sanur, an English-speaking guide, all entrance fees (Diamond Beach, Atuh Beach, Thousand Islands viewpoint, Molenteng Tree House), and a local lunch.</p></div>
                </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <aside>
                <div class="pricing-card">
                    <h3 style="color:var(--primary-color);font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:10px;">Package Pricing</h3>
                    <p style="color:#666;font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:20px;">All-Inclusive Private Tour</p>
